    "rationale": "Repair of a structured-output defect that silently disabled schema enforcement for every OpenAI-style provider.\n\nThe agent decision schema is written for validation and carries bounds, defaults, and bare `const` values. Ollama accepts that document directly and enforces it as a generation grammar, so the locally served arms were schema-constrained. OpenAI's strict structured-output mode accepts a narrower subset and rejects the whole request rather than ignoring what it cannot express; the first rejection was `schema must have a 'type' key` at `properties.request.properties.workload`, whose `{\"const\": \"one_shot\"}` carries no `type`. The client's fallback then retried in free-form `json_object` mode, which succeeded, so the run completed with no error while every request was unconstrained: 156 of 156 calls in the gated frontier arm and 183 of 183 in its ablation ran without schema enforcement.\n\nThe visible consequence was concentrated in CLARIFY. Unconstrained, the model returned the right decision in the wrong shape: field names it invented (`clarification`, `clarifying_question`, `questions`) and questions as bare strings rather than objects, each of which the parser rejected. All four benchmark items that require the agent to formulate a clarification failed in every arm, while all eight decided by the deterministic topology gate passed in every arm. The agent had identified the ambiguity and asked the correct question; the pipeline discarded it.\n\nThree changes, all in files this lock covers:\n\n1. `src/agentic_anex/llm_clients/strict_schema.py` (new) rewrites a validation schema into the strict subset: unsupported keywords dropped, `const` expressed as a typed single-value enum, every object requiring all of its properties, and previously optional properties made nullable. The rewrite only removes constraints the strict subset cannot express, never adds or relaxes semantics, and every dropped constraint is still enforced when the response is parsed.\n\n2. `src/agentic_anex/llm_clients/openai_compatible_client.py` sends the rewritten schema. Ollama continues to receive the original document.\n\n3. `src/agentic_anex/orchestration.py` reads the nulls a strict mode must emit for a property it cannot omit: null for a field carrying a contract default means \"not stated\", and a null clarification list means \"none asked\". The rule that CLARIFY must ask something, and every domain check the dropped bounds used to duplicate, are unchanged and covered by tests.\n\n`scripts/preflight_openai_arm.py` now probes with the real agent schema. It previously probed with a simpler schema of its own, which the provider accepted under strict mode while rejecting the real one; that is why the preflight reported the frontier arm as schema-constrained when it was not.\n\nScope: the sealed benchmark is untouched. Requests, gold labels, the authoring lock, the prompts, and the topology catalogue all carry the same hashes as in evaluation_lock_v3.json. Only the agent changed. Results produced under evaluation_lock_v3.json remain valid as results of that pipeline and are retained for comparison; results produced under this lock are not comparable to them arm by arm and must be reported as a separate campaign.",
    "results_produced_under_the_base_lock_remain_valid_for_that_lock": true,
    "unchanged_file_count": 75
  },
